---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
	<main class="page-narrow">
		<article class="card text-card prose">
			<p class="overline">About</p>
			<h1>About the atlas</h1>
			<p>The Övör Mongol Atlas is an interactive historical atlas of Inner Mongolia (Övör Mongol) from the late Qing dynasty to the early People's Republic of China, with the Timeline Map running from 1890 to 1950. It covers the people, places, groups, states and events of that period, including the Inner Mongolian autonomy movements of the 1930s and the Japanese-sponsored Mengjiang territory.</p>
			<p>Entries are built from scholarly and archival sources: academic monographs, journal articles, contemporary press coverage, and primary accounts by participants and outside observers. Where sources disagree on a date, a name, a location or the reading of an event, the atlas records the disagreement and does not quietly pick a side. Conflicts that cannot be settled are marked as such in the entries, with what each source claims.</p>
			<p>The <a href="/map">Timeline Map</a> draws borders only as they stood in each year, on 1 July, from period sources. Each entry with a place or territory shows a small version of that map, linked to the full map at the same year.</p>
			<p>See the <a href="/editorial-principles">Editorial Principles</a> for how entries are written and sourced.</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.text-card {
		padding: 2rem 2.25rem 2.25rem;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0.3rem 0 1rem;
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.2;
	}

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.text-card {
			padding: 1.25rem;
		}
	}
</style>
